Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for Next.js App Router project

## What was implemented:

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the colour-zen project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes made:

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- Package version: Latest version from npm registry

### 2. Analytics Configuration
Modified `/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
- Integrated `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag in the root layout
- Placed the Analytics component after the children content, following Next.js App Router best practices

### 3. Files Modified:
- `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree

## Implementation Details:

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Used the `@vercel/analytics/next` import path for optimal Next.js integration
- Placed the Analytics component at the root layout level to track all pages
- Maintained existing code structure and formatting
- Preserved all existing functionality including fonts and CSS imports

## Verification:

✅ Build completed successfully - no errors
✅ TypeScript compilation passed
✅ Package installation completed without issues
✅ Lock file updated correctly
⚠️ Linter found pre-existing issues in other files (unrelated to Analytics integration)

## Notes:

- The Analytics component will start collecting data once the application is deployed to Vercel
- No additional configuration is required for basic analytics tracking
- The component is lightweight and will not impact application performance
- Analytics data can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard after deployment
